            "ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In the 2012 multicenter placebo-controlled depression trial, paroxetine and venlafaxine XR improved depressive symptoms without worsening motor function; this describes that trial rather than proving all SSRIs effective in PD. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3324323/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d4e4d10f63a375f3d506144ae2adb78744f40f1a68ae785fde1a14c6323f6c6e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:394d8d948dc71b5be6744fa4d6afbb84a9ac70179dff68b43589ba7817c65092",
            "ev:92eded0b00b1b3f548d83a4d2c8edccdc0a3a72841f33cce5e79f2b43a2a39b9",
            "ev:a3df7fcec1aed488ba0a140d9ce1b078ef685342685f733fc81e942ac45272dc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Apathy involves diminished motivation and goal-directed behavior and can occur independently of depression; its characteristic indifference differs from depressive dysphoria or hopelessness, despite overlap between the syndromes. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12261265/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:86745a8fa6048bbc85414cdc990ac695f9256cff016a78990f36cf2f196c0986",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:74bc8dd8bc627a65014aed929e4bbbe3a82800c0088244eeea4b2c63494a7c15",
            "ev:f993e12856efa3c849bc31eff0d927ae660c5b11447cb0d8e0050986047ae894"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7738499/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Venlafaxine XR reduced depressive symptoms versus placebo in the 12-week SAD-PD trial without worsening motor function; the 2019 MDS review rates venlafaxine clinically useful for PD depressive symptoms. This establishes trial and review findings, not comparative superiority over all antidepressants. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3324323/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d537e5f951bfa080dd69a095748f1779066330a07733aca4b8d72c2069f9191c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0df6cb691254dc545e9214b0791f6bfaeeab8437b3853d115a9a0027559a9c41",
            "ev:3f93107b2208d5c1b73b683cb866089dca482fb49dc16dd739f86f10b69faa33",
            "ev:a615cc8508432b224236057c4d5b487e6d68504b5fb1bcacab59d4f2a19e282c",
            "ev:a9dee5845c62927bb6ffee6db04968b4f747f7a74b735962c84e88a459d98e9a"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The 2024 German guideline says physical interventions might be offered for apathy, but its evidence discussion describes small mixed trials, including no significant dance-therapy effect versus active controls. Apathy exercise evidence is less established than a broad efficacy claim would imply. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/",
