      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:f58064bd2b81a193de76b70841d5a0976b9861d9d577760f284681ee1812592f",
      "text": "The cited sources treat PD psychosis, depression, anxiety and apathy as distinct problems with distinct assessment and treatment choices. Psychosis care includes checking medical and medication triggers; clozapine and pimavanserin have stronger efficacy evidence than quetiapine. Depression has antidepressant and CBT trial evidence. Anxiety CBT results depend partly on the outcome scale. Apathy can occur independently of depression, and treatment findings from small or selected populations need careful qualification. These distinctions matter because apparent benefit in one syndrome or short trial does not establish benefit or long-term safety across all four.",
